      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nA logical error in the `_checkMintCap` function within the `LatentSwapLogic.sol` library effectively disables the minting cap for small markets. The function uses a logical AND `(&&)` operator where a logical OR `(||)` is required, allowing users to mint tokens far in excess of the intended limits. This can be exploited to manipulate market prices, create worthless synthetic tokens, and potentially drain \nvalue from the protocol.\n\n## Vulnerability \nThe `_checkMintCap` function is designed to limit the size of a single mint operation relative to the market's total size. For small markets `(where marketBaseTokenSupply <= (1 << noCapLimit))`, the intention is to prevent a mint that is either larger than the current supply or larger than a very high absolute limit `(FixedPoint.Q96)`.\n\n```solidity\nfunction _checkMintCap(\n    uint256 marketBaseTokenSupply,\n    uint256 eTWAPBaseTokenSupply,\n    uint256 mintAmount,\n    uint8 noCapLimit\n) internal pure {\n    // ...\n    unchecked {\n        if (marketBaseTokenSupply <= (1 << noCapLimit)) {\n            // This check is flawed.\n            if ((mintAmount > FixedPoint.Q96) && (mintAmount > marketBaseTokenSupply)) {\n                revert LSErrors.E_LEX_MintCapExceeded();\n            }\n        } else if (\n            // ... logic for large markets\n        ) {\n            revert LSErrors.E_LEX_MintCapExceeded();\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n The condition should be changed to use a logical OR (||) to correctly enforce the cap.\n```solidity\nif (marketBaseTokenSupply <= (1 << noCapLimit)) {\n            if ((mintAmount > FixedPoint.Q96) && (mintAmount > marketBaseTokenSupply)) {\n            if ((mintAmount > FixedPoint.Q96) || (mintAmount > marketBaseTokenSupply)) {\n                revert LSErrors.E_LEX_MintCapExceeded();\n            }\n```",
